WEBVTT

00:22.410 --> 00:25.500
...Iroshito and Kakuya, right?

00:25.500 --> 00:26.040
Yeah.

00:26.040 --> 00:27.700
If it's all three of them, they can win.

00:27.700 --> 00:28.600
Yeah.

00:28.600 --> 00:31.000
That Hiroshima card is amazing!

00:31.000 --> 00:32.170
Yeah, I know.

00:32.170 --> 00:33.250
Is Kyoko-chan coming too?

00:33.360 --> 00:34.200
Huh, is that so.

02:45.030 --> 02:48.810
Oh yeah, I was e-mailing Michiru, and then...

02:49.990 --> 02:50.950
Oh, no!

02:57.990 --> 02:59.620
Did you sleep well?

03:00.000 --> 03:00.930
Yes.

03:01.780 --> 03:04.370
I was asleep before I even realized it.

03:04.370 --> 03:07.040
I see. That's good to hear.

03:17.650 --> 03:19.660
Well then, I'm off.

03:20.460 --> 03:21.200
Okay.

03:23.840 --> 03:24.450
Morning.

03:24.560 --> 03:26.460
Good morning.

03:30.150 --> 03:31.380
Midorikawa-kun!

03:31.850 --> 03:33.570
What have you been doing until now?

03:33.900 --> 03:34.570
Went for a walk.

03:35.080 --> 03:37.110
What is that huge thing?

03:37.410 --> 03:39.890
On the same occasion, I went to ride some waves.

03:40.690 --> 03:43.030
Aren't you becoming a trainee?

03:43.270 --> 03:44.740
Don't do things as you please!

03:46.110 --> 03:50.050
That's why I finished quickly and came back early.

03:50.850 --> 03:56.050
We're here to look after you on behalf of your parents.

03:56.050 --> 03:57.410
Yeah.

03:57.410 --> 03:59.410
I hope you'll refrain from doing selfish things.

03:59.980 --> 04:00.890
I...

04:01.450 --> 04:04.090
Ah, Sayori-chan, let's just leave it at that for today.

04:04.390 --> 04:06.010
It's only his first day after all.

04:06.010 --> 04:07.290
Besides, I'm hungry.

04:07.520 --> 04:11.910
Don't go calling me Sayori-chan. It's Sayori-obaasan to you!

04:13.140 --> 04:14.440
Midorikawa-kun!

04:14.650 --> 04:16.060
You just laughed, didn't you?

04:18.710 --> 04:20.550
"You just laughed, didn't you?"

04:23.840 --> 04:26.360
So, how were the waves today?

04:29.160 --> 04:32.830
The waves were a bit weak, but it was fun.

04:33.480 --> 04:36.490
It was really hard to do a barrel.

04:37.270 --> 04:39.690
I caught a few proper closing waves though,

04:40.060 --> 04:41.700
so I was able to make two barrels.

04:44.380 --> 04:46.900
Hey now, was that even Japanese?

04:51.870 --> 04:52.940
Yo!

04:53.070 --> 04:54.500
Good morning!

04:54.650 --> 04:57.850
The printer ink and fax paper were both refilled.

04:57.850 --> 04:59.300
That's my Fune-chan.

04:59.660 --> 05:01.350
Always working quickly.

05:02.060 --> 05:04.950
Sensei, there's no use trying to flatter me.

05:04.950 --> 05:06.390
Good morning!

05:06.500 --> 05:09.240
Ah, a new student?

05:10.170 --> 05:11.330
Please to meet you,

05:11.450 --> 05:14.870
I'm Fune, the person who helps out at the office.

05:15.160 --> 05:16.340
Fune-san...

05:17.730 --> 05:20.210
The kanji for "sound" and "wind", said as Fune.

05:17.730 --> 05:20.210
風 (kaze, fuu) = wind, 音 (oto, ne) = sound, 風音 = fune

05:20.420 --> 05:21.080
Yes.

05:21.330 --> 05:23.600
Ah, I'm Suzuki Sora.

05:23.720 --> 05:25.800
Pleased to meet you, Sora-chan.

05:26.170 --> 05:27.660
Same to you.

05:29.620 --> 05:33.270
Today's request will also be Sora's first magic client.

05:33.690 --> 05:34.420
Yes.

05:35.650 --> 05:39.050
The client is Motohashi Mami-san, age 55.

05:39.770 --> 05:41.340
Her request is always the same.

05:41.610 --> 05:43.460
Always the same?

05:44.060 --> 05:48.160
Generally, any magical requests require approval, but not this one.

05:48.850 --> 05:52.200
Motohashi-san knows many politicians and bureaucrats.

05:53.930 --> 05:56.040
The request involves opening a vault.

05:56.410 --> 05:59.050
All the mages in the district have been asked to help.

05:59.460 --> 06:00.950
Of course, she always makes the same request.

06:01.770 --> 06:03.140
The same request...

06:07.110 --> 06:12.140
Today your magic client will be Yamaguchi Makoto-san, age 32.

06:12.730 --> 06:15.910
His magic request involves memories...

06:17.190 --> 06:18.440
Midorikawa-kun.

06:18.700 --> 06:20.210
Ah, sorry.

06:24.810 --> 06:25.860
Oh, that's right.

06:26.210 --> 06:27.390
I suppose it can't be helped.

06:30.390 --> 06:32.110
I heard about it from your father.

06:32.620 --> 06:37.810
Midorikawa-kun, you've only learned recently that you are of mage descent, right?

06:40.040 --> 06:41.890
You've never been able to use magic.

06:42.280 --> 06:44.150
I understand if you're insecure about it.

06:45.770 --> 06:49.630
However, you definitely have the blood of a mage flowing through your body.

06:50.110 --> 06:52.030
So don't run away from this fact.

06:52.430 --> 06:53.140
I...

06:57.190 --> 07:01.150
The instructor can decide on the requests a student handles.

07:01.770 --> 07:02.480
Therefore...

07:02.480 --> 07:05.420
I would like to fulfill Motohashi-san's request.

07:06.240 --> 07:08.310
She can be quite a handful...

07:09.220 --> 07:12.430
I think that I can do something if I meet her...

07:13.850 --> 07:14.560
All right then.

07:14.870 --> 07:17.940
Today's magic request will be at Motohashi-san's place.

07:18.110 --> 07:18.710
Okay!

07:20.190 --> 07:22.160
I'll do my best!

07:28.090 --> 07:29.850
You'll be late again.

07:30.010 --> 07:30.510
Huh?

07:30.510 --> 07:31.160
Ah!

07:34.990 --> 07:35.580
Um...

07:36.510 --> 07:37.530
Thank you.

07:37.530 --> 07:42.840
Sure.

07:42.840 --> 07:43.600
I-I...

07:44.090 --> 07:44.700
Um...

07:44.980 --> 07:46.110
This stuff sure looks difficult.

07:46.650 --> 07:48.030
I don't even get half of it.

07:50.730 --> 07:54.270
Yesterday, I fell asleep while reading my friend's mail.

07:55.410 --> 07:59.040
I got scolded after I called my good friends in Nagasaki.

07:59.040 --> 07:59.890
What?!

08:00.060 --> 08:01.990
You mean you're not allowed to call your friends?

08:04.480 --> 08:07.550
Well, it was because I was calling in the middle of the night...

08:08.050 --> 08:09.420
Ah, so you're a night owl too?

08:09.940 --> 08:16.230
No, but after hearing about my client today, I couldn't sleep.

08:16.720 --> 08:18.600
No need to worry about that.

08:19.140 --> 08:24.300
If you talk with the instructor and understand the request, you'll be fine.

08:24.780 --> 08:27.590
After that, it's all about applying what you know.

08:27.720 --> 08:31.000
Seems like you know what you're talking about, Kuroda Koji.

08:31.120 --> 08:33.700
It's pointless to worry about it, that's all.

08:33.700 --> 08:37.330
Isn't this your first time fulfilling a magic request?

08:37.540 --> 08:38.370
Of course.

08:40.080 --> 08:42.080
As usual, you have some amazing self-confidence.

08:42.480 --> 08:44.210
What about you, then?

08:44.320 --> 08:48.460
Well, it's just magic training. Piece of cake, right?

08:49.100 --> 08:51.150
What? You're just the same.

08:51.810 --> 08:53.510
Everyone's so amazing.

08:53.510 --> 08:55.430
They're so relaxed.

08:55.430 --> 08:56.870
That's not true.

08:57.410 --> 08:58.070
Um,

08:58.530 --> 09:00.640
my first magic client is...

09:00.830 --> 09:04.060
you can say her reasons are somewhat special...

09:04.060 --> 09:07.240
She has a huge family and for some reason she always requests the same magic-

09:07.030 --> 09:10.410
Mages must respect the confidentiality of their client's request.

09:11.370 --> 09:15.760
Out of concern for your clients, please do not speak casually about their matters.

09:16.840 --> 09:18.000
Man, scary...

09:18.210 --> 09:19.440
Oohata-kun!

09:19.630 --> 09:21.080
Stay quiet!

09:21.320 --> 09:22.330
Sorry.

09:22.720 --> 09:23.870
Good morning, everyone.

09:23.870 --> 09:26.010
Good morning.

09:26.580 --> 09:29.490
It appears that everyone is on time today.

09:30.520 --> 09:32.050
I'll begin with today's lecture.

09:33.080 --> 09:38.750
If there's anyone here who has used magic in public, please raise your hand.

09:50.840 --> 09:52.320
Well then, Suzuki Sora-san.

09:52.820 --> 09:53.510
Y-yes!

09:54.650 --> 09:59.210
You performed magic the day before your training began, isn't that right?

09:59.710 --> 10:00.280
Yes.

10:00.670 --> 10:02.410
What kind of magic did you use?

10:02.930 --> 10:03.780
Well...

10:04.170 --> 10:07.820
I was walking around the city and I heard a very loud noise...

10:08.090 --> 10:10.060
After that, a truck came falling down...

10:10.340 --> 10:13.740
I just said "stop" and my body reacted to it naturally.

10:14.860 --> 10:16.660
You saved lives, didn't you?

10:16.980 --> 10:17.730
Yes.

10:18.250 --> 10:19.910
That was before the magic training class...

10:20.480 --> 10:25.040
But... I know I did lots of magic that I shouldn't have done.

10:25.900 --> 10:26.550
Um...

10:26.630 --> 10:27.250
But...

10:26.860 --> 10:31.700
The use of magic before undergoing training is not against the law.

10:31.700 --> 10:32.530
Oh.

10:34.690 --> 10:37.000
Your parents were mages.

10:37.870 --> 10:40.150
Until you turn sixteen and undergo training,

10:40.150 --> 10:43.120
your parents are responsible for supervising your magic use.

10:43.800 --> 10:50.040
Any magic performed by anyone here in public before then is not punishable by law.

10:50.620 --> 10:51.830
That's good to hear.

10:52.130 --> 10:52.940
However!

10:53.450 --> 10:55.880
If you now use magic beyond your client's needs without proper authorization,

10:55.880 --> 10:58.920
the Magic Bureau will judge you and pass appropriate punishment.

10:59.280 --> 11:01.050
Please remember this well.

11:01.050 --> 11:02.720
That seriously scared me.

11:03.020 --> 11:05.490
I will now hand out the class notes.

11:11.140 --> 11:13.320
Will Midorikawa-kun be all right?

11:14.600 --> 11:16.130
Midorikawa-kun?

11:16.460 --> 11:19.440
At yesterday's practical skills exam, he wasn't able to do anything.

11:19.440 --> 11:21.910
And today he's just been reading.

11:23.820 --> 11:26.230
Will he be able to do today's training?

11:28.550 --> 11:32.140
Yamabuki-san, you've been watching Midorikawa-kun pretty closely.

11:32.490 --> 11:33.500
Is that so?

11:34.480 --> 11:37.440
I think Yamabuki-san will become a first class mage.

11:37.900 --> 11:38.850
What's that?

11:39.570 --> 11:41.510
How can you make such an assumption?

11:41.870 --> 11:45.320
Pardon me, but will you try not to get in my face all the time?

11:45.730 --> 11:49.170
Do you know of the saying, "big fish in a little pond"?

11:49.460 --> 11:55.300
The big fish in the little pond does not know of the ocean, but he knows a lot about the blue sky.

11:55.770 --> 11:57.500
You're seriously not cute at all.

12:00.630 --> 12:02.740
Using magic is like riding a bicycle.

12:02.740 --> 12:03.170
Heh.

12:03.170 --> 12:06.050
Once you get the hang of it, you can do it eventually.

12:06.450 --> 12:09.190
But there are many types now...

12:09.190 --> 12:09.770
Huh?

12:09.770 --> 12:12.360
Bicycles! I meant bicycles.

12:12.500 --> 12:13.200
Oh.

12:13.420 --> 12:15.170
Do you know what pigments are?

12:15.170 --> 12:15.810
No.

12:16.020 --> 12:17.040
Oh, okay.

12:18.650 --> 12:20.930
Morishita is really weird.

12:22.670 --> 12:25.970
Will Midorikawa-kun be all right with this magical training?

12:25.970 --> 12:27.300
Sora-chan is really kind.

12:27.580 --> 12:28.980
Ah, um...

12:29.230 --> 12:30.590
Hiyori-chan...

12:30.870 --> 12:34.310
But for now, you should concentrate on your own tasks.

12:34.590 --> 12:37.210
Yes, I will do my best!

12:37.350 --> 12:39.020
All right, good answer.

12:47.780 --> 12:50.080
We're from the Magic Bureau.

12:50.260 --> 12:51.540
I'm Hara Seiichirou.

12:51.840 --> 12:55.280
We've been expecting you, please come in.

12:57.090 --> 13:00.200
This is my first time seeing such a huge house.

13:02.240 --> 13:04.920
How many people live here?

13:04.920 --> 13:08.680
Right now, only the mistress and I live here.

13:08.930 --> 13:11.530
All alone in this big house...

13:12.880 --> 13:15.020
Oh, it's Hara-san today.

13:15.570 --> 13:16.420
Pleased to meet you.

13:16.930 --> 13:18.400
You are free to go.

13:18.580 --> 13:19.810
Yes, mistress.

13:20.610 --> 13:22.670
Today I came here to accompany her.

13:22.790 --> 13:23.570
Oh?

13:24.120 --> 13:27.880
My trainee, Suzuki Sora-san will be the one actually handling this.

13:28.260 --> 13:29.450
Pleased to meet you.

13:31.020 --> 13:33.620
I'm Suzuki Sora.

13:33.620 --> 13:35.140
Um... about your request...

13:34.520 --> 13:37.500
Come with me then, Suzuki-san.

13:37.500 --> 13:38.190
Okay.

13:40.470 --> 13:42.850
The entrance is a bit low. Do be careful.

13:43.530 --> 13:44.130
Okay.

13:48.540 --> 13:50.100
Now then, do your thing.

13:52.360 --> 13:56.020
Motohashi Mami-san, about today's magical request of opening the vault...

13:56.020 --> 13:57.810
Hurry up and open it now.

14:00.250 --> 14:01.440
What's the matter, child?

14:01.740 --> 14:03.150
Aren't you a mage?

14:03.510 --> 14:04.890
Having such a young child do it...

14:05.920 --> 14:06.990
Sora-chan...

14:07.130 --> 14:10.430
Unlocking magic isn't difficult to do.

14:10.790 --> 14:11.720
Then do it.

14:13.130 --> 14:15.160
Motohashi-san, you don't have the key, yet...

14:15.160 --> 14:17.580
...why do you always keep having this safe locked?

14:25.710 --> 14:27.770
The request involves opening a vault.

14:28.460 --> 14:30.850
All the mages in the district have been asked to help.

14:31.440 --> 14:32.980
Of course, she always makes the same request.

14:33.590 --> 14:35.450
The same request...?

14:36.030 --> 14:40.850
Once the vault is opened, she will ensure the contents are there,

14:41.730 --> 14:45.060
and then have the vault locked again.

14:45.650 --> 14:47.080
Since she doesn't have the key, she makes this request over and over.

14:47.830 --> 14:50.280
What's inside the vault?

14:50.650 --> 14:53.740
Well, no one knows...

14:59.930 --> 15:02.450
To fulfill Motohashi-san's magic request,

15:02.710 --> 15:05.320
I will now use magic on the vault to open it.

15:06.900 --> 15:08.250
By the power of iron...

15:10.620 --> 15:13.050
open this door...

15:16.690 --> 15:19.690
You should have just done this from the very beginning, for God's sake.

15:20.910 --> 15:22.940
Well then, the both of us will wait outside.

15:23.440 --> 15:25.200
Sora-chan, let's go outside-

15:25.340 --> 15:25.930
Hey...

15:31.120 --> 15:32.010
What are you doing?

15:32.270 --> 15:33.030
Get away!

15:33.030 --> 15:34.820
Leave this place!

15:36.290 --> 15:36.990
Sora-chan!

15:37.340 --> 15:38.180
Stop!

15:39.470 --> 15:40.950
What is with her?

15:43.740 --> 15:44.580
I...

15:45.150 --> 15:48.310
I... just wanted Motohashi-san to come outside!

15:48.960 --> 15:49.730
Come outside?

15:50.110 --> 15:52.340
Living in such a big house with just two people...

15:52.760 --> 15:54.090
You're still living...

15:54.400 --> 15:56.320
It's so sad watching her live like this.

15:56.470 --> 15:57.310
Sora-chan,

15:58.010 --> 16:00.640
we cannot interfere with the lives of our clients.

16:00.890 --> 16:03.140
But, if this keeps up...

16:03.480 --> 16:05.550
That is not a mage's duty.

16:05.680 --> 16:06.310
But!

16:14.930 --> 16:16.800
Come, let's go back.

16:22.140 --> 16:24.720
Sorry that I wasn't able to spend time with you today.

16:31.350 --> 16:33.280
Sora-chan, this is...

16:34.040 --> 16:38.510
I didn't use any movement magic. I used destructive magic instead.

16:39.560 --> 16:42.040
If it cannot lock again...

16:42.620 --> 16:44.390
This wasn't Motohashi-san's wish.

16:44.390 --> 16:45.260
I know that.

16:45.390 --> 16:49.620
She would call a mage to open the vault and then look at the photo albums.

16:50.060 --> 16:53.650
That's right, those are very important to me.

16:54.600 --> 16:57.640
No matter how many mages you summon, you'll never be able to go back.

16:58.040 --> 17:00.120
You won't be able to see the people in the photos.

17:00.420 --> 17:01.850
It is fine that way.

17:02.410 --> 17:03.860
Don't let your life stop here.

17:04.270 --> 17:05.620
Let's get out of this house!

17:05.620 --> 17:06.470
Sora-chan!

17:06.650 --> 17:08.630
If you keep being imprisoned within the vault...

17:08.630 --> 17:09.840
...time will be stopped!

17:10.080 --> 17:10.780
Shut up!

17:11.020 --> 17:13.730
What's important is not in the vault!

17:14.490 --> 17:16.210
The most important thing is...

17:16.890 --> 17:18.580
...your own life!

17:21.740 --> 17:24.120
My own life?

17:29.560 --> 17:33.500
Motohashi-san's husband was a famous politician, right?

17:33.670 --> 17:38.470
Yes. Thanks to him, I was able to visit many countries.

17:39.340 --> 17:41.620
Every time he returned, we would have a coming-home party.

17:42.160 --> 17:44.040
We didn't have time to take a rest.

17:44.700 --> 17:45.860
Is that your daughter?

17:46.010 --> 17:50.380
Maiko went to study abroad in England and got married there.

17:50.810 --> 17:53.550
She hasn't returned in over a year.

17:53.550 --> 17:55.000
England looks wonderful.

17:55.490 --> 17:57.940
I really like Peter Rabbit.

17:58.100 --> 18:02.220
The author lived at a place called Hilltop by the Lake.

18:02.220 --> 18:03.970
Sora-chan knows a lot.

18:03.970 --> 18:05.890
I really want to go to England.

18:06.770 --> 18:10.400
After the death of my husband, I wasn't able to go.

18:11.070 --> 18:12.410
What a waste!

18:12.870 --> 18:15.270
There are so many places I want to see.

18:15.560 --> 18:18.150
Then Sora-chan, would you like to go with me?

18:19.450 --> 18:21.900
I think it would be boring with only me.

18:22.570 --> 18:24.410
Where is your mother, Sora?

18:24.410 --> 18:25.960
She's at Biei in Hokkaido.

18:26.510 --> 18:28.250
She lives alone right now.

18:28.250 --> 18:29.160
I see.

18:29.160 --> 18:31.290
My dad passed away.

18:31.290 --> 18:36.360
Normally, you should refer to him as your "father," instead of your "dad."

18:31.290 --> 18:36.360
In Japan one refers to their own father by 'chi-chi' rather than 'Oto(u)-san'

18:36.530 --> 18:38.400
Ah, I'm sorry!

18:38.620 --> 18:39.300
Um...

18:39.450 --> 18:41.550
my father passed away.

18:42.130 --> 18:43.620
But Chao is there.

18:43.870 --> 18:44.890
Chao-san?

18:44.890 --> 18:47.130
Yes, he's our family's dog.

18:47.310 --> 18:48.930
Really energetic.

18:49.110 --> 18:50.240
Even more than yourself?

18:50.360 --> 18:51.030
Yes!

18:51.330 --> 18:53.890
Then that should be just as heartwarming for your mother.

18:56.320 --> 19:01.200
Even when old man Masaru invites us over for dinner, she doesn't go.

19:01.680 --> 19:03.130
It would be lively.

19:03.970 --> 19:06.730
That I can somewhat understand.

19:06.920 --> 19:07.940
How come?

19:08.060 --> 19:10.200
Being alone within another household...

19:10.410 --> 19:12.300
It does become lonely.

19:12.820 --> 19:13.680
Alone...

19:13.970 --> 19:16.510
Even if it was fun at that moment...

19:16.990 --> 19:20.200
It becomes very depressing afterwards when you're alone again.

19:20.960 --> 19:24.810
Therefore, it's better to be alone from the start.

19:24.990 --> 19:28.010
There's no way you'd be better off alone.

19:28.620 --> 19:29.680
Sora-chan.

19:32.430 --> 19:34.160
Please don't say things like that.

19:34.530 --> 19:39.060
"It's better to be alone from the start." Don't say such sad things.

19:39.470 --> 19:41.160
Don't cry, Sora-chan.

19:41.940 --> 19:47.050
It's because you have a family that you have your precious memories and photo albums.

19:47.680 --> 19:48.580
That's true.

19:48.850 --> 19:49.700
That's true.

20:00.100 --> 20:01.210
Gouta-kun, wait!

20:04.250 --> 20:05.410
Gouta-kun!

20:10.770 --> 20:11.610
Gouta-kun!

20:13.290 --> 20:15.420
I've been reading about magic theory all morning.

20:15.640 --> 20:17.650
I even tried moving the balls in the pachinko machine.

20:17.910 --> 20:20.600
I tried various things, but in the end I couldn't do a single thing.

20:22.050 --> 20:26.160
Only a few can control their magic easily on the first try.

20:26.160 --> 20:28.970
Am I really a mage?

20:29.110 --> 20:32.630
Yes, without a doubt, you are.

20:32.820 --> 20:33.940
That's ridiculous.

20:34.190 --> 20:36.300
Telling me this all of a sudden just causes me more problems.

20:36.810 --> 20:40.320
Sometimes you just have to accept what fate has dealt you.

20:41.660 --> 20:43.220
What the hell do you know?!

20:44.050 --> 20:44.940
Then come home.

20:46.380 --> 20:47.320
Are you coming home?

20:48.600 --> 20:50.550
You're just like your father.

20:59.160 --> 21:00.000
Huh?

21:00.270 --> 21:04.220
Yesterday, there was a woman that was here playing the guitar...

21:04.460 --> 21:05.110
Huh?

21:05.110 --> 21:06.000
Who?

21:06.400 --> 21:08.730
I know quite a bit of the people here.

21:10.320 --> 21:11.340
I'm sorry!

21:12.530 --> 21:15.720
I got carried away and acted selfishly...

21:22.900 --> 21:24.060
Hara-sensei.

21:24.220 --> 21:24.780
Hmm?

21:25.420 --> 21:26.950
The sky in Tokyo is very colorful.

21:27.100 --> 21:28.480
It's different from Biei.

21:28.860 --> 21:29.630
I see.

21:30.360 --> 21:32.590
But, both are beautiful.

21:33.540 --> 21:34.260
Yeah.

23:06.560 --> 23:08.860
I've never dated a boy before.

23:08.860 --> 23:12.430
So it's hard for me to understand how guys feel.

23:13.790 --> 23:15.310
Next time, Gouta.

23:15.770 --> 23:19.260
I get dizzy just looking at conveyor belt sushi...
